      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not sure you need make_pair here. I think you could just use the initializer-list syntax:\n\n  return {createWifiStatus(...), std:vector...};\n\nThe initializer list will be used to call the std::pair\u003cWifiStatus, std::vector\u003chidl_string\u003e\u003e ctor. And the types of the parameters are already correct, so no conversion is necessary. (make_pair would be useful if we needed to explicitly convert one or more of the pair elements.)\n\nSimilarly throughout this file.\n\n\n(In fact, I think you can even go so far as to nest the initializer lists, and just say\n\n  return {createWifiStatus(...), {}};\n\nBut explicitly initializing a vector is fine, too.)",
